From: Oreon Packaging Team <packaging@oreonhq.com>
Subject: [OREON] configure: sanitize skipdirs/noconfigdirs before $notsupp

Strip any word starting with '-' from skipdirs and noconfigdirs before the
loop that builds $notsupp. That stops bogus "*** This configuration is not
supported in the following subdirectories: -MMD -MP ..." output when a
compiler-flag string leaks into a directory list (PR124547 class breakage).

--- configure
+++ configure
@@ -10680,6 +10680,24 @@
    skipdirs="${skipdirs} ${target_configdirs}"
 fi
 
+# Oreon: strip tokens starting with dash from skipdirs/noconfigdirs (defensive, PR124547-related).
+__oreon_sd=""
+for __oreon_d in $skipdirs; do
+  case $__oreon_d in
+  -*) ;;
+  *) __oreon_sd="$__oreon_sd $__oreon_d" ;;
+  esac
+done
+skipdirs=$__oreon_sd
+__oreon_sd=""
+for __oreon_d in $noconfigdirs; do
+  case $__oreon_d in
+  -*) ;;
+  *) __oreon_sd="$__oreon_sd $__oreon_d" ;;
+  esac
+done
+noconfigdirs=$__oreon_sd
+
 # Remove the entries in $skipdirs and $noconfigdirs from $configdirs,
 # $build_configdirs and $target_configdirs.
 # If we have the source for $noconfigdirs entries, add them to $notsupp.
